Known gaps (checked 2026-11-16 against master; signatures against NoesisPython.dll via
openoesis' spec/api.json):

- API signatures: 128 stubs still take *args, 176 functions of the current API don't exist,
  and 9 take fewer arguments than the DLL allows: rapi.swapEndianArray, imageDecodeRawPal,
  imageNormalMapFromHeightMap, imageFromMortonOrder, imageKernelProcess, decryptAES,
  loadTexByHandler, rpgSetUVScaleBias, rpgBindUserDataBuffer.
- rapi.setPreviewOption("setAngOfs", "0 180 0") (default preview rotation) is stored but the
  viewer only applies setAnimSpeed.
- rpgSetStripEnder is a stub: strips restart only on 0xFFFF / 0xFFFFFFFF.
- rpgSetUVScaleBias is stored on the meshes but not applied.
- imageDecodePVRTC (rapi/pvr.py) doesn't really decode: it returns colour A of each 8x8 area
  as an image 1/8 the width and height. openoesis (formerly noesis_rs) has a port of Noesis'
  own decoder (crates/openoesis-core/src/image_codecs/pvrtc.rs) to follow if this is ever needed.
